# Full Stack Open – Part 0: Fundamentals of Web Apps

This repository contains my solutions for **Part 0** of the **Full Stack Open** course by the University of Helsinki.

## 📝 About

Since I already have prior knowledge of **HTML, CSS, and JavaScript**, I was able to complete most of Part 0 relatively quickly. Although many of the concepts were already familiar to me, this section served as a valuable refresher on the fundamentals of web applications, including the client-server model, HTTP requests, and the differences between traditional web applications and Single Page Applications (SPAs).

## 📂 Exercises

### 0.4 – New Note Diagram
A Mermaid sequence diagram illustrating what happens when a user creates a new note using the traditional Notes application.

### 0.5 – Single Page App Diagram
A Mermaid sequence diagram showing the events that occur when a user opens the Single Page Application (SPA) version of the Notes application.

### 0.6 – New Note in Single Page App Diagram
A Mermaid sequence diagram demonstrating how a new note is created in the SPA version without reloading the page.

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- Mermaid
- Markdown
- Git
- GitHub

